title: "pallet-conviction-voting: make Tally::add and Tally::remove atomic on overflow/underflow"
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `Tally::add` and `Tally::remove` mutated `self.support` before checking the following
    `self.ayes`/`self.nays` `checked_add`/`checked_sub`, so a later overflow or underflow returned
    `None` while `self.support` had already been changed, leaving the tally partially updated. The
    `Split` and `SplitAbstain` variants had the same issue. All new field values are now computed
    before any assignment, so a failed `add`/`remove` leaves the tally unchanged.
crates:
- name: pallet-conviction-voting
  bump: patch
